    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0465" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/5–1445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of
                            State to President Truman
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-14">May 14, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been informed informally by the War Department that the United States
                    lines in Czechoslovakia extend from a point west of Carlsbad south through the
                    Sudeten area to Pilsen and then southeast to the Austrian frontier at a point a
                    few miles west of Budweis. The American occupation includes Pilsen and extends
                    northeast nine miles beyond that city to a point less than forty miles from
                    Prague. I am also informed that the United States forces are at present
                    withdrawing in Czechoslovakia although there are no specific orders from SHAEF
                    to do so. The withdrawal is being made by Commanders under general orders to
                    make “local adjustments”.</p>
                <p>In view of the important political considerations advanced in the memorandum of
                    May 5, a copy of which is attached,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d455-f1"/>, I earnestly
                    recommend that you consider requesting the Joint Chiefs of Staff to instruct
                    SHAEF through proper channels to hold the line in Czechoslovakia that our troops
                    now occupy, including the city of Pilsen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
